# Corners: outer brand radius, fixed md inside

Three corner sizes, all CSS-variable tokens defined once in tools/tokens.ts → packages/tokens/theme.css:

- **Outer** surface of a block (card, band, panel, plan, form card, FAQ tile, media panel): `rounded` / `rounded-lg` = `--radius` (2.5rem = 40px, from the Figma frame).
- **Inside** a block, every inner corner is the fixed `--radius-md` = `calc(var(--radius) * 0.5)` = **20px**, independent of the padding around it. Use the semantic aliases (all = `--radius-md`):
  - `rounded-nested`: inner tiles, rows, inner cards (settings rows, disclosure / fieldset cards).
  - `rounded-field`: input, select, textarea (recipes). On an `h-10` field 20px is half the height, so a single-line field reads as a pill; a textarea gets 20px corners.
  - `rounded-dense`: tables and data/detail lists with a header row (the container clips with `overflow-*`, so the header row follows its corners; cell text `text-sm`, cells `whitespace-nowrap`, the container scrolls) and notices: alerts (recipe), notifications, toasts, the cookie banner.
  - Plain `rounded-md` is the same value where no semantic role fits.
- **Preview frame** (design apps only, `.ds-frame`, not part of a block): `--preview-radius` 8px (`rounded-preview`) on `--preview-surface` (`bg-preview`, a `color-mix` tint of `--primary` over `--background`), defined in the apps' generated brand.css.

Rules:
- Pills stay pills: buttons and badges keep `rounded` / `rounded-full`; circles (icon badges, avatars, FAQ arrow) keep `rounded-full`. Buttons inside notices keep their own shape.
- Media fills its box edge to edge (`size-full object-cover`, anchor `object-top` for app screens): no padding on the media container, no radius or ring on the image; the container's `overflow-hidden` + its own radius clip the corners (blog cards, hero/feature split art, social proof panel, app gallery tiles).
- There is no padding-derived (concentric) radius any more: the former `surface-pad-N` / `nested-pad-N` utilities, `--surface-pad`, `--nested-pad` and `--radius-floor` were removed. Do not reintroduce `calc(outer − padding)` per surface.
- Arbitrary values (`calc`) exist only in the token definitions (tools/tokens.ts → theme.css). To retune every inner corner, change `--radius-md` (or point the aliases at another token) there and run `bun run tokens`.
